  "development_findings": [
    "The old control used unrestricted DuckDB settings and kept scan, build, and comparison allocations in one process.",
    "Adding the 192 MB database setting alone reduced memory but did not pass the complete 768 MiB test limit.",
    "Splitting build and comparison alone still left scan allocations in the build process.",
    "Separating original scan, original database build/audits, and read-only comparison passed the limits without increasing them.",
    "The first saved SQL memory check failed after earlier fixture allocations. Running saved data first and checking every sequential phase fixed the test; the focused rerun passed.",
    "A corruption-test transaction prevented DuckDB from detaching its control catalog. The test now restores its temporary view after each comparison without wrapping ATTACH/DETACH in that transaction."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "RSS limits are test gates, not an OS-enforced ceiling.",
    "Synthetic test dispatcher is excluded; each isolated controller and all sequential operation workers are counted.",
    "The 32-snapshot validation and existing import tests have limited memory margin.",
    "Only eight saved snapshots were compared. Full archive, all 40 historical exceptions, and production integration remain untested.",
    "The v1 control still builds its complete selected sample; full-history memory and temporary disk use need separate validation.",
    "Default production history commands retain their previous scanner and database settings.",
    "Source retention, backup removal, and production cutover remain outside this phase."
  ]
